fluenced O'Bannon's work on alien he  would find his quote spiritual warriors  and then put them together in one big  room to work out a movie structure later  O'Bannon would use the same strategy to  brainstorm about alien bringing together  fuss Gieger and cartoonists Mobius and  Ron Cobb to hash out the designs their  little sci-fi horror project script  struggles ultimately Brandywine  productions agreed to produce the film  for 20th Century Fox with Ridley Scott  in the director's chair  but the Nostromo still had some  turbulence ahead according to O'Bannon  producers a David giler  and Walter hell wanted to completely  redo his script so that's exactly what  they did  according to gala he and Hill added the  feminist elements everyone is talking  about we gave the characters texture  functions in O'Bannon Strauss they were  totally different military types or men  we changed all the dialogue every word  of it O'Bannon the original screenplay  featured a xenomorph and the wrecked  ship and that's about where the  similarities for the finished  and Tails and Gaia's rewrites added  Ripley and Dallas and the rest of the  gang not to mention the whole vast  corporate conspiracy subplot and the  entire concepts for human looking  Androids an idea that was already an  alien cornerstone by the first sequel  [Music]  thank you but bizarrely some drafts also  had a time travel based plot line  featuring Jack the Ripper Hercules and  Genghis Khan like a Magic Treehouse book  with murderous chester birthing aliens  then there's the alien fat against all  odds Scotland has teams somehow made  despite all the confusion as artists  Christopher Foss splitted the den of  geek poor old Dan O'Bannon the bloke  whose concept it was just got absolutely  shafted I kind of got the impression  that Ridley was quietly going his own  way trying to get on with it and get it  done  shipshape the Nostromo the dark  claustrophobic spaceship where all the  alien action takes place is practically  another character in the movie and Chris  fuss and Ron Cobb were essential to the  creation of the vessel but the final  result didn't come right away the team  worked on the design for five whole  months pretty much the whole time the  producers were trying to find a director  for the movie and some of those designs  got weird first had endless spaceship  designs  suggesting submarines at diesel  locomotives Mayan interceptors  Mississippi riverboats and a jumbo space  arks but in the end they were simply too  outlandish for the producers to get on  board the Nostromo's final design that  came from one of Ron Cobbs simple of  sketches and even then Ridley Scott made  the ships modeler get rid of Cobbs  original yellow color scheme in favor of  the flat grader made it into the film  casting chaos before Sigourney Weaver  got the part of Ripley none other than  Meryl Streep was on the short list of  candidates to be offered the role Streep  is of course ridiculously talented and  alien probably would have been just fine  with her in the lead role but fate  intervened in 1978 Streep's romantic  partner actor John Cazale passed away  and nobody felt comfortable  interrupting her morning to make the  offer as it turns out  Ripley wasn't even sigourney weaver's  first choice she said in an interview  actually the part I wanted to play was  Lambert Veronica Cartwright part in the  first script I read lumber just cracked  jokes the whole time that's the  character I could identify with and  while Weaver wanted the path of Lambert  Veronica Carter I was dead set on  playing Ripley it was only just before  shooting began that scraps right was  told their roles have been switched  obviously the decisions all worked out  from the end but it's interesting to  consider how close we were to getting a  completely different movie silly scenes  Wibbly Scott works hard to preserve the  lessons more aesthetic that's made alien  so terrifying and that meant cutting a  lot of scenes from the final film some  of the biggest cuts were made because  they looked kind of stupid  for example Lambert's death is haunting  because most of it is implied and  off-screen the camera cuts away just  before the alien get sir so we don't  actually see what happens but her death  was filmed it just looked way too cheesy  by the same token bretch death in the  final film is terrifying but the  extended cut of that scene is borderline  absurd  I'm not come over to Academical legacy  for a sci-fi horror creature feature  alien gets a surprising amount of love  in the academic world case in points  June 2017 saw the publication of a book  called alien and philosophy a collection  of essays on all things alien it's heavy  stuff but it just goes to show there's  more to the xenomorph or the facehugger  a chest burster and a man in a crocodile  suit if the grotesque imagery  state-of-the-art special-effects and a  storage production aren't enough to  build a compelling film theory thesis  that maybe or those Freudian themes will  do the trick  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our youtube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know your love to  [Music]
 

